$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.2 Synthesis of intermediate 3-chloro-4-substituted phenoxy-nitrobenzene
(1a-1j) 0.11 mol substituted phenol was added to a 250 mL three-necked
flask, and heated to melt, then added 0.10 mol KOH, stirred until the
water produced in the reaction was released to obtain phenolate. The
reaction flask was equipped with a thermometer and a reflux condenser
tube, followed by the addition of 1,2-dichloro-4-nitrobenzene
[substituted phenol : KOH : 1,2-dichloro-4-nitrobenzene = 1.2 : 1.2 : 1
(molar ratio)], then heated to inner temperature of 150 °C, and reacted
for 1-2.5 h, monitored by TLC. After reaction, the mixture was washed
with 5 % NaOH solution for three times at 80-100 °C to remove excess
phenol. Then the mixture was washed with water for two times at 80-100
°C, adjusted pH to neutrality with dilute hydrochloric acid. The hot
solution was poured into cold water, cooled and suction filtered, then
dried over to give the intermediate 1a-1j (yield 71 % - 85 %). 1a, 85 %
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, thermal
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 7-chloro-4-hydroxy-6-(phenoxy)-3-quinolinecarboxylic acid
ethyl ester derivatives and determination of their activity as
coccidiostats
