$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of new monomer: 2,6-bis(4-chloroformylphenoxy)benzonitrile
(ClPOBN). To a 250-mL round-bottomed flask equipped with a mechanical
stirrer, a thermometer, and nitrogen inlet and out tubes, and a
Dean-Stark trap, 72 mmol of p-hydroxybenzoic acid, 144 mmol of KOH, 70 mL
of dimethyl sulphoxide (DMSO), and 55 mL of toluene were added. The
reaction mixture was heated to 140-150°C until no further water was
azeotropically distilled from the reaction mixture, and then temperature
was raised to 170°C to remove toluene. After being cooled to 40°C,30 mmol
of 2,6-difluorobenzonitrile was added and the reaction mixture was heated
to 185-195 °C and stirred at this temperature for 8 h. After cooling to
room temperature, the reaction mixture was dissolved in water and
hydrochloric acid was added, and then the product was precipitated. The
solid product was washed with water and recrystallized from the mixture
of ethyl alcohol and water thrice. 2,6-bis(4-carboxyphenoxy)benzonitrile
(CPOBN). Yield 85%; purity 96%. m.p. 311-312 °C. IR(KBr): 3429 (OH), 2235
(CN), 1695 (C═O), 1605, 1578, 1506 (C═C); 1245 (-O-). 1H NMR (DMSO-d6),
δ: 8.07-8.09 (4H, H1); 7.02-7.04 (4H, H2); 7.21-7.22 (2H, H3); 7.31 (1H,
H4). Elemental analysis calculated for C21H13NO6; C, 67.2; H, 3.47; O,
25.6. Found: C, 67.3; H, 3.54; O, 25.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dean-Stark trap used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Study on synthesis of novel soluble aromatic polyamides with pendant
cyano groups
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yu, Yikai; Cai, Mingzhong; Zhang, Yuejun
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Polymer Bulletin (Heidelberg, Germany) (2010), 65(4), 309-318

