$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of the monomer A mixture of DMAc (80 mL), toluene (20 mL),
anhydrous potassium carbonate (3.649 g, 26 mmol), p-hydroxyldiphenylamine
(8.89 g, 48 mmol), 2,6-difluorobenzonitrile (2.78 g, 20 mmol) were added
into 250 mL three-necked round-bottom flask. Then it was heated at 130 °C
under nitrogen with stirring for 2 h to remove the water by azeotropic
distillation with toluene. After that, the toluene was removed. The
mixture was heated to reflux for 8 h to ensure completion of the
reaction. Then the solution was cooled to room temperature and poured
into distilled water to precipitate the product. The crude product
filtered from the solution was washed by distilled water and ethanol for
several times, respectively, filtered and dried under dynamic vacuum at
45 °C for 24 h. Yield 85%. MALDI-TOF-MS: The calculated mass-charge ratio
for C31H23N3O2 is 469.5. And the ion peak at the mass-charge ratio 469.7
was observed in the experiment. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6,<delta>): 8.25 (s, 2H,
He), 7.48 (t, 1H, Ha, J= 8.50 Hz), 7.24 (t, 4H, Hg, J=7.87 Hz), 7.15 (d,
4H, Hd, J= 9.01 Hz), 7.11 (d, 4H, Hf, J= 9.02 Hz), 7.08 (d, 4H, Hc, J=
7.68 Hz), 6.84 (t, 2H, Hh, J=7.29 Hz), 6.48 (d, 2H, Hb, J= 8.50 Hz). FTIR
(in KBr, cm-1): 3369 (υNH), 3033 (υCH), 2231 (υC≡N), 1598 (υC=C of
benzenoid rings), 1506 (υC=C of benzenoid rings), 1325 (υC-N), 1252
(υC-O-C), 833 (δCH), 744 (δCH), 692 (δCH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
