$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for oxacalixarenes 1, 6, 11:
The linear trimer (0.34 mmol) and resorcinol derivative (0.34 mmol) were
dissolved in MeCN (10 ml). To this was added Et3N (0.34 mmol), and the
mixture was stirred at 75°C for 3.5 hrs. After cooling, the reaction
mixture was poured into a mixture of water and MeOH (1:1).The
precipitated crude product was collected by filtration, washed with cold
MeOH, dried in vacuo. Product as pale yellow solid in 65-90% yield. 11:
This symmetrical compound was prepared in a one pot reaction, using 1eq
of resorcinol derivative and 1eq of 1,5-difluoro-2,4-dinitrobenzene. 85%
yield. 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3): 9.05 (s, 2H, ArH), 7.76 (s, 2H, ArH), 5.31
(s, 2H, ArH), 4.38 (q, 2H, J=7.1Hz, COOCH2 ), 1.39 (t, 3H, J=7.1Hz,
COOCH2 CH3 ). 13C NMR (400MHz, CDCl3): 163.11, 155.06, 154.94, 135.38,
132.60, 127.09, 122.63, 102.45, 94.44, 62.76, 14.23. HRMS (ESI-) calcd.
for C30H17N4O16I2, 942.8729; Found, 942.8727.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
