$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
2,3,13,14-tetradecyloxy-5,11,16,22-tetraaza-6,10,17,21-tetrachloro-7,9,18,20-tetraoxo-8,19-dicyanoenneacene
(CDPzN, 1) 1,4-dichloro-7,8-bis(decyloxy)phenazine-2,3-diol 2 (593 mg, 1
mmol) and K2CO3 (690 mg, 5 mmol) were placed in a two-necked round bottom
flask under nitrogen atmosphere. DMF (20 mL) was added. After stirring
for 1 h at room temperature, tetrafluoroterephthalonitrile (90 mg, 0.45
mmmol) was added and the mixture was heated at 100°C for 3 days. The
mixture was allowed to cool down to ambient temperature before pouring
into deionised water (200 mL). Yellow crystals were obtained which were
recrystallized from chloroform and dried in vacuum. 500 mg 1 (yield: 85
%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.38 (s, 4H), 4.19 (t, J = 6.5 Hz, 8H),
1.94-1.83 (m, 8H), 1.50-1.28 (m, 56H), 0.89 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 12H). IR:
2240 cm-1 (CN) 13C NMR failed to obtain due to poor solubility of CDPzN.
HR-MS: Formula: C72H89N6O8Cl4, Calc. Mass, 1305.5496, Found, 1305.4839.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis, Characterization, and Nonvolatile Ternary Memory Behavior of a
Larger Heteroacene with Nine Linearly Fused Rings and Two Different
Heteroatoms
