$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,5-[(3,5-Bismethoxycarbonyl)phenoxy]phthalonitrile (3). A mixture of
4,5-dichlorophthalonitrile 1 (1.0 g, 10.15 mmol), 5-hydroxyisophthalate 2
(4.28 g, 40.60 mmol), and K2CO3 (16.6 g, 0.12 mol) in DMF (60 mL) was
stirred at 65 °C for 24 h. The reaction mixture was poured into icewater
to give a white-brown precipitate, which was extracted with CHCl3 (5 ×
100 mL). The organic extracts were dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and
concentrated under vacuum to give a yellow oil. After recrystallization
from methanol, the title compound 3 was obtained as a white solid (2.35
g, 85%), mp 191-192 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 8.56 (s, 2H, Ar-H), 7.83 (s,
4H, Ar-H), 7.32 (s, 2H, Ar-H), 3.97 (s, 12H, CH3). FTIR (solid) 1727.1
(C=O), 2235.1 (CN) cm-1. MS (MALDI) m/z 544.13 (M+H+). Anal. Calcd. for
C28H20N2O10: C 61.77, H 3.70, N 5.15. Found: C 61.46, H 3.76, N 4.99.
