$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Ethyl
2-Cyclopropyl-6-fluoro-4,7-diphenyloxyquinoline-3-carboxylate (10a) A
mixture of phenol (0.95 g, 10.1 mmol), 6 (1.5 g, 4.81 mmol), anhydrous
K2CO3 (1.39 g, 10.1 mmol), and DMF (15 ml) was stirred at 100 °C for 16
h. When it was cooled to room temperature, the solid was isolated by
filtration and washed with ethyl acetate. The resulting mixture was
transferred to a separatory funnel, and ethyl acetate and water were
added. The organic layer was separated, washed with brine, dried over
Na2SO4, and concentrated to dryness to give an off-white solid, which was
recrystallized from n-hexane to give 10a (1.85 g, 87%) as a colorless
powder. Ethyl
2-Cyclopropyl-6-fluoro-4,7-di-(4-fluorophenyloxy)quinoline-3-carboxylate
(10b) Colorless powder, yield 85%; Compounds 10b-10e and 13a-b were
prepared in the similar manner otherwise the reaction temperature
mentioned in Tables 1 and 2. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.53 (d, J=11.2
Hz, 1H), 7.25 (d, J=7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.12-7.10 (m, 4H), 7.01-6.96 (m, 2H),
6.88-6.84 (m, 2H), 4.17 (q, J=7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.20-2.16 (m, 1H), 1.26-1.21
(m, 2H), 1.15 (t, J=7.2 Hz, 3H), 1.03-0.99 (m, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, regioselective, product depends on stoichiometry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Regioselective SNAr Reaction of Poly-halo-quinoline-3-carboxylates with
Phenol, Thiophenol, or N-Methylaniline
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhao, Shikui; Zhou, Weicheng
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2011), 41(1), 20-32

