$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of
4-aryloxy-2,6-dibromo-1-nitrobenzenes 5 (general procedure). Phenol (2
mmol) and K2CO3(0.28 g, 2 mmol) was added to a solution of
2,6-dibromo-4-fluoro-1-nitroso benzene (4) (0.56 g, 2 mmol) in DMSO (7
mL). The mixture was stirred at 40-50 °C for 30-40 min. The resulting
solution was cooled in an ice bath. The precipitate was filtered, washed
with water, and dried. 2,6-Dibromo-4-(4-tert-butylphenoxy)nitrosobenzene
(5b). Yield 0.70 g (85%). m.p. 130-132°C (EtOH). Found (%): C, 46.66; H,
3.49; N, 3.34. C16 H15NO2Br2. Calculated (%): C, 46.48; H, 3.63; N, 3.38.
1H NMR, δ: 1.32 (s, 9 H, Bu t); 7.21 (d, 2 H, H(2´), H(6´), J = 8.7 Hz);
7.41 (s, 2 H, H(3), H(5)); 7.55 (d, 2 H, H(3´), H(5´), J = 8.7 Hz). MS,
m/z (I rel(%)): 413 [M]+(100), 411 (31), 398 (39), 368 (53), 287 (29),
91(33), 77 (28), 74 (23), 57 (21), 44 (32), 30 (100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 4(6)-aryloxy- and 4-arylthio-2,1,3-benzoxadiazoles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kuznetsova, A. S.; Gornostaev, L. M.; Stashina, G. A.; Firgang, S. I.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Chemical Bulletin (2013), 62(9), 2079-2082

