$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.3 Coupling of 2,4-dibromophenol with fluorobenzaldehydes :
2,4-Dibromophenol (5.0 mmol) and the fluorobenzaldehyde (C-8~9) (5.0
mmol) were dissolved in DMAC. Anhydrous Na2CO3 (5.0 mmol) was added, and
the reaction mixture was heated at reflux for 1.5~2 h. CH2Cl2 and water
were added to the cooled reaction mixture; the organic layer was
separated and washed with aqueous NaOH (1 mol/L) and water. The crude
product was purified by silica gel with n-hexane/ethyl acetate
(dichloromethane) as eluent. Yield 85%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
