$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of ethyl 4-(4-nitrophenoxy)benzoate (3): K2CO3 (55.2 g, 0.4
mol) was suspended in dry CH3CN solution (50 mL), ethyl 4-hydroxybenzoate
(16.6 g, 0.1 mol) was added, and the reaction mixture was heated to
refluxing temperature, then to this stirred suspension, a solution of
1-fluoro-4-nitrobenzene (15.5 g, 0.11 mol) in freshly distilled CH3CN (50
mL) was added over a period of 0.5 h from a dropping funnel. After the
addition was completed, the reaction mixture was refluxed and stirred
overnight. After filtering, the solvent was evaporated to give a grown
powder, which was washed several times with water. The product was
purified by crystallization with hexane/ethyl acetate to give 3. Pale
yellow crystals, yield (24.3 g, 84.4%). m.p. 68~70°C (Lit. mp 67~68°C)
(Consiglio et al., 2000).
