$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (3-Methoxy-4-(4-nitrophenoxy)phenyl)methanol (23) [5]: To a solution of
1-fluoro-4-nitrobenzene (4.5 g, 32.6 mmol) in DMF (50 mL) were added
K2CO3 (18.1 g, 131 mmol), compound 22 (6.4 g, 41.5 mmol), and 18-crown-6
(100 mg, 0.4 mmol). The mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 12
h. After the reaction completed (TLC monitoring), the reaction mixture
was diluted with CH2Cl2 (150 mL), washed with water (100 mL), 1N NaOH (20
mL × 3), water (until neutral to litmus paper), brine, and dried over
Na2SO4. Evaporation of the organic solvent afforded compound 23 (7.5 g,
84%).
