$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,3-Bis(4-nitrophenoxy)naphthalene (1,3-BNPON). A mixture of 3.0 g (1.87
mmol) of 1,3-dihydroxynaphthalene, 5.54 g (3.9 mmol) of
p-fluoronitrobenzene, 5.54 g (4.1 mmol) of potassium carbonate and 30 mL
of dry DMF was refluxed at 120°C over an oil bath for 3 h. The mixture
was then cooled and then poured into 200 mL of methanol-water (1:1 by
volume). The precipitate was washed with methanol and warm water, and
then it was collected by filtration and driedin vacuum to obtain 6.8 g of
dinitro compound (1,3-BNPON). It was recrystallized from glacial acetic
acid. Yield: 6.3 g (83.7%), as a yellow crystallized. melting point
124-125°C. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6): δ = 8.23-8.27 (m, 4H, phenylene), 8.02-8.04
(d, 1H, naphthalene, J=8.0 Hz), 7.91-7.93 (d, 1H, naphthalene, J=8.4 Hz),
7.68 (s, 1H, naphthalene), 7.50-7.66 (m, 2H, naphthalene), 7.24-7.29 (m,
1H, naphthalene, 4H, phenylene). 13C NMR (DMSO-d6): δ = 162.83, 162.45,
152.03, 151.61, 142.62, 135.04, 128.07, 127.99, 126.53, 126.27, 126.19,
123.92, 121.30, 117.98, 117.41, 114.30, 114.08, 111.42. Anal. Calc. for
C22H14N2O6 (402.29) C, 65.63%; H, 3.48%; N, 6.96%. Found: C, 65.65%; H,
3.55%; N, 6.68%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel organo-soluble aromatic polyimides derived from unsymmetrical
1,3-bis(4-aminophenoxy)naphthalene and aromatic dianhydrides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Wen-Tung; Wang, Kun-Li
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Macromolecular Research (2010), 18(9), 821-827

