$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 4-(dodecyloxy-biphenyl)-4′-nitrophenyl ether (b). Into a
250-mL round-bottomed flask was placed a mixture of DMF (100 mL), a (8.80
g, 0.025 mol), p-chloronitrobenzene (4.25 g, 0.027 mol), and K2CO3 (13.82
g, 0.100 mol). After the mixture had been stirred at 150 °C for 8 h, the
mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature and then poured into
distilled water with vigorous stirring. The pale-yellow solid precipitate
was filtered, washed with ethanol, and then dried. Consequently about
10.04 g of purified compound b (yield: 84 %) were obtained. 1H NMR
(CDCl3-d): δ (ppm) 7.61, 7.52, 7.06, 6.99 (m, 8H, Ar-H of biphenyl),
8.22, 7.13 (m, 4H, ArH-NO2), 4.00 (t, 2H, -CH2-O-), 1.46-1.86 (m, 20H,
-(CH2)10-), 0.98 (t, 3H, methyl). FT-IR (KBr, pellet), cm-1: 2918, 2850
(C-H), 1608, 1499 (aromatics), 1590, 1349 (NO2), 1254, 1164 (C-O-C). HRMS
(ESI-TOF) m/z: [M + Na]+ calcd for C30H37NNaO4: 498.2615; found:
498.2628.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of novel soluble polyimides containing triphenylamine groups
for liquid crystal vertical alignment layers
